What you see here is the relocation of computer networking infrastructure (an entire server room) from Riverside City College's MLK Building's server room to 
the new BLCIS building's network operation center room (NOC room), contributing to the de-racking, re-racking, moving, labeling, documenting, 
performing cable management and installation of 9 servers, 9 Cisco switches, 9 ISR routers, 2 control switches, 5 UPS units, and 27 Mac Minis for
the NETLAB+ virtual environment so that RCC students can access networking resources such as virtual machines, and virtual labs remotely. 
A total of 5-month planning phase and 3 months of execution by a group of cyber assistants (7 people including Jason Patrick Salerno).


